cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use nefi, please cite the two papers it implements (listed under "references").
  The software itself can be cited with the metadata below.
title: "nefi: Neural-Field Inversion"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "CAB Lab, Princeton University"
    website: "https://cablab.scholar.princeton.edu"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-09-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ContinuumCoder/NEFI"
url: "https://continuumcoder.github.io/NEFI/"
abstract: >-
  nefi recovers hidden physical fields from a single measurement without training data. The
  unknown is represented by a coordinate neural field or any other parameterization, pushed
  through a differentiable forward model of the instrument as a hard constraint, and optimized
  with an adaptive coarse-to-fine, frequency-annealed curriculum. The library generalizes the
  NeTMY and NeFTY papers and ships diagnostics, a benchmark protocol with an inverse-crime guard,
  auto-tuning, edge refinement, visualization and seventeen registered problems from 1-D to 3-D.
keywords:
  - inverse problems
  - neural fields
  - differentiable physics
  - scientific machine learning
  - computational imaging
references:
